# Environment notes

- Windows 11, PowerShell 7. Commands run via `run_commands`; `grep`/Unix tools unavailable, use `Select-String`.
- GitHub CLI (`gh`) is installed (v2.98.0) and authenticated. Prefer `gh` over raw REST calls
  for GitHub operations (e.g. `gh run watch <id> --repo JochemKuipers/JuiceWRLD-API-DL --exit-status`,
  `gh run view`, `gh pr`).
- `uv` is installed. Run tests with `.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q` (or `uv run pytest`).
- After editing `pyproject.toml` (esp. version), run `uv lock` — CI uses `uv sync --locked`.
- Push multiple git refs sequentially in separate commands; batched pushes in one command
  list sometimes race and report "Everything up-to-date".
